WEBVTT

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:02.267
Start with the average-age condition.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:05.122
This is the same scalar pattern from earlier.

00:00:05.122 --> 00:00:08.917
Run it and note which patients are above the overall average.

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:12.727
These rows become candidates for the final combined query.

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:17.127
Testing the condition separately makes later debugging much easier.

00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:21.437
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:26.292
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:29.562
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.537
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:33.537 --> 00:00:40.182
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:40.182 --> 00:00:46.122
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:48.320
not only whether the statement executes.
